            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two numbers have a sum of 58. One number is two more than the other number. Find the two numbers.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "28 and 30.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the larger number and $y$ the smaller number.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+y&=58 &&(1)\\\\x-y&=2 &&(2)\\end{align*}$$\nAdding equations (1) and (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}2x&=60\\\\x&=30\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting $x=30$ into equation (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}30+y&=58\\\\y&=28\\end{align*}$$\nThe two numbers are 28 and 30.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
